          </table></div>

          <h2>What is this registry counting, and what is it not?</h2>
          <p>A row here is a building that OpenStreetMap contributors have tagged as a data
            center in {sec.state}. That is a mapping record, not a licence, a filing or an
            operator disclosure, so the count is a floor in both directions: a facility nobody has
            mapped is absent, and a mapped building may be a small network node rather than a
            campus. The registry says what is documented, which is the only claim a crowd-built
            source supports.</p>
          <p>The IT megawatt column is stricter still. A figure appears only where the operator
            published it on its own specification page, so a dash means unpublished rather than
            zero, and a state total assembled from this column is the published subset rather than
            the state's capacity. Colocation providers publish spec sheets far more often than
